Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["  XXZ bulk with Exchange edge coupling  ", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"f10950bb-f06b-6740-ad71-8c53d15855e7"],

Cell["\<\
  L total spins: edges A=1 and B=L, bulk M={2,...,L-1}. No magnetic fields \
are added. This notebook is self-contained. Evaluate its initialization cells \
once; the two static scans, state dynamics and channel dynamics then run \
independently. All model parameters are editable within their own run. g must \
be nonzero; Delta may be zero. These .m files use separate named contexts. \
Evaluate the Begin cell first: it saves the caller search path and restricts \
symbol lookup to System` while this file context is active. Evaluate the \
final cell to restore the path. Evaluate all required definition cells before \
a chosen run; run cells are executable. Get evaluates every run.  \
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"e80fffdb-678d-d643-af4c-7d1dcdd49db4"],

Cell[BoxData[""], "Input",ExpressionUUID->"8e14acf6-c98a-5e49-8cf7-1d8d8044ecd3"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Begin", "[", "\"\<XXZExchange`\>\"", "]"}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"XXZExchange`savedContextPath", "=", "$ContextPath"}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"$ContextPath", "=", 
   RowBox[{"{", "\"\<System`\>\"", "}"}]}], ";"}]], "Code",
 CellChangeTimes->{4.0013848652217865`*^9},
 CellLabel->"In[1]:=",ExpressionUUID->"ff7ed560-38dc-af4a-95c8-58e21a410e67"]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
  1. Statics: complete sector eigenpairs, entropies and IPR  \
\>", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"5b522698-94aa-a941-99b5-b2521aec1fa6"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["  1.1 Definitions shared by all four chapters  ", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"10a41a4d-c467-4146-b852-49512df7fa26"],

Cell["\<\
  Initialization cells contain definitions only. They do not start a scan, \
diagonalize a model, choose an initial state, plot, or export. Their \
benchmark conventions are S=sigma/2, hbar=1, bit 0=up, natural-log entropy, \
edge basis {00,01,10,11}. Both end bonds replace the usual XXZ end bonds.  \
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"74263a3b-e27e-0a48-b0ef-949b5b3584de"],

Cell["\<\
  H = J Sum[j=2,...,L-2](Sjx S(j+1)x + Sjy S(j+1)y + Delta Sjz S(j+1)z) + g \
(S1x S2x + S1y S2y + S(L-1)x SLx + S(L-1)y SLy). J and g have energy units. \
In the exchange case the spin-flip matrix element is g/2.  \
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"a48a21fa-64a5-694d-97c3-8641c597ae53"],

Cell["\<\
  Exchange resolves total magnetization m and reflection R; at m=0 it also \
resolves spin flip F. Opposite-m spin-flip partners share a static panel with \
separate labels and data. Neither Delta=+1 nor Delta=-1 restores full-chain \
SU(2), because the end bonds contain only XY exchange. At Delta=0 the \
Hamiltonian is free fermionic (conditional bulk for ZZ); the benchmark \
spin/spatial classification stays valid, with additional conserved mode \
occupations and possible degeneracies. It is not a classification of every \
integrability charge. No degenerate energy vectors are silently mixed or \
pooled across the listed sectors.  \
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7868e103-8909-be47-9d80-e0931f4b410c"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["  Utilities, spin operators and Hamiltonian guards  ", "Subsubsection",ExpressionUUID->"ec4d7fad-0946-2b4f-a7b4-7d786dff268d"],

